"[2610.23048] Distill Until Divergence: Error-Truncated Hindsight Distillation for Agentic RL (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23048)\nciteturn41211view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23048\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 Oct 2026]\nL9: # Title:Distill Until Divergence: Error-Truncated Hindsight Distillation for Agentic RL\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Yibin Huang , cite6†Conghui Zhu L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Distill Until Divergence: Error-Truncated Hindsight Distillation for Agentic RL, by Yibin Huang and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Long-horizon interaction requires agents to make multiple decisions in a changing environment. Outcome-based GRPO lacks fine-grained guidance for intermediate decisions. Recent methods distill completed trajectories into reusable skills and use hindsight-conditioned OPD to provide dense token-level credit.\nL17: However, skill-induced probability shifts do not necessarily represent reward-aligned credit; especially after an erroneous action changes subsequent interaction states, skill-conditioned supervision may become mismatched with the current state.\nL18: To address this mismatch, we propose \\methodname{}, which routes two complementary hindsight skills according to trajectory outcomes and error boundaries: Positive skills capture successful workflows to reinforce successful trajectories and pre-error decisions, while Negative skills capture failure-specific corrections to target decisive errors. The post-error suffix is optimized exclusively by GRPO, retaining outcome-based learning without extending potentially mismatched hindsight supervision.\nL19: Extensive experiments demonstrate competitive task performance and support effective fine-grained credit allocation.\nL20: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2610.23048 [cs.AI]\nL22:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2610.23048v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL23:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.23048†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Yibin Huang [cite12†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:28:05 UTC (549 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled Distill Until Divergence: Error-Truncated Hindsight Distillation for Agentic RL, by Yibin Huang and 1 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite7†View PDF L36:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite13†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite14†view license L40: \nL41: ### Additional Features\nL42: \nL43:   * cite15†Audio Summary L44: ### Current browse context:\nL45: \nL46: cs.AI\nL47: \nL48: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L49: \nL50: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2026-10 L51: \nL52: Change to browse by:\nL53: \nL54: cite21†cs L55: \nL56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * cite22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L59:   * cite23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L60:   * cite24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71: \nL72: ### Bookmark\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL75: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Bibliographic Explorer (cite25†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL80: \nL81: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL82